# Firebase service account credentials. This file is full administrative access
# to the Firebase project — it can mint a token for any user and read every
# document. It belongs outside the repository, and never in a commit.
*service-account*.json
firebase-adminsdk-*.json
/storage/firebase/

# google-services.json and GoogleService-Info.plist are deliberately NOT ignored.
#
# They hold client identifiers, not secrets: they ship inside every installed
# copy of the app, and anyone can read them out of an APK. Ignoring them would
# also be self-deception here, because firebase_options.dart carries the same
# values and is tracked — while the app would stop building for anyone who
# cloned the repository.
#
# What actually protects the project is the restriction attached to each key —
# package name plus signing certificate on Android, bundle id on iOS — set in
# the Google Cloud console. That is the control worth checking.
